**8. Scope Limitation**

The above scope shall cover transactions, activities, systems, and controls implemented at the level of the project during the period under review.

The auditor is expected to exercise professional judgement and may extend the scope of the audit where additional procedures are considered necessary to obtain sufficient and appropriate audit evidence or where material risks, irregularities, weaknesses, or other significant matters are identified.

